  "term": "recreational therapy",
  "definition": "Recreational therapy is a therapeutic approach that uses structured activities, such as arts and crafts, music, time with animals, sports, or drama, to support the physical and emotional needs of people with illness or disability. It also aims to build skills used in everyday living.",
